1
00:00:00,533 --> 00:00:01,633
10 月 8 号早上
Morning of October 8

2
00:00:01,633 --> 00:00:04,566
我照常一边冲咖啡一边刷 AI 新闻
Making coffee, scrolling AI news as always

3
00:00:04,666 --> 00:00:07,800
刷到一条Anthropic 发了新模型
when I saw Anthropic had released a new model

4
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:09,666
Claude Haiku 5点5
Claude Haiku 5.5

5
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,766
官方说平均跑下来
They said on average

6
00:00:11,766 --> 00:00:14,133
比上一代便宜了大约 百分之75
it's about 75% cheaper than the last one

7
00:00:14,366 --> 00:00:16,533
我第一反应是好事啊
My first thought was great news

8
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:18,000
账单要变薄了
my bill's getting thinner

9
00:00:18,066 --> 00:00:19,800
结果就在同一个星期
Then that same week

10
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:22,200
同一家公司又上了一个新功能
the same company rolled out a new feature

11
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:24,566
一句话就能拉起 1000 个 AI
where one line could spin up 1,000 AI agents

12
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:26,133
同时帮你干活
all working for you at once

13
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,000
他们自己在说明里提醒
Even their own docs warn you

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,266
这个功能会消耗大量的 token
this feature burns through a ton of tokens

15
00:00:30,433 --> 00:00:31,600
token 是什么
So what's a token

16
00:00:31,666 --> 00:00:34,100
国家数据局有个说法挺形象
China's National Data Administration put it well

17
00:00:34,166 --> 00:00:36,333
它就像互联网时代的流量
it's like data traffic in the internet era

18
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:38,800
AI 读一段字写一段字
AI reads some text, writes some text

19
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:40,100
都按它算钱
all billed by the token

20
00:00:40,366 --> 00:00:41,566
2024 年初
Early 2024

21
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,600
咱们国家一天用掉的 token
the tokens we used nationwide each day

22
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,700
是 1000 亿
were 100 billion

23
00:00:44,933 --> 00:00:47,600
到今年 3 月是 140 万亿
By this March, it hit 140 trillion

24
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:49,566
两年一千多倍
More than 1,000 times in two years

25
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:52,200
单价一直在掉用量一直在涨
Unit price kept falling, usage kept climbing

26
00:00:52,366 --> 00:00:54,166
掏出去的钱也跟着涨
and so did the money spent

27
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,600
东西越便宜反而花得越多
The cheaper it got, the more we spent

28
00:00:56,633 --> 00:00:58,300
这事听着别扭
Sounds off, I know

29
00:00:58,366 --> 00:00:59,966
可早在一百六十年前
But 160 years ago

30
00:00:59,966 --> 00:01:01,966
就有人把它写进了书里
someone had already put it in a book

31
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,733
这里是像素呼吸
This is Pixel Breath

32
00:01:03,866 --> 00:01:05,300
今天聊聊
Today, let's talk about

33
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:08,133
AI 越便宜你为什么花得越多
why the cheaper AI gets, the more you spend

34
00:01:09,266 --> 00:01:10,566
先说句公道话
To be fair

35
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:13,366
觉得降价就能省钱一点都不傻
thinking a price cut saves money isn't dumb at all

36
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:16,100
菜便宜了买菜就花得少
Veggies get cheaper, you spend less

37
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:19,300
油价降了加满一箱就少掏几十块
Gas gets cheaper, a full tank costs a bit less

38
00:01:19,466 --> 00:01:20,633
但这笔账里
But that math

39
00:01:20,633 --> 00:01:22,733
藏着一个没说出口的前提
hides an unspoken assumption

40
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:24,466
你买的量不变
that you buy the same amount

41
00:01:24,866 --> 00:01:27,566
菜还是那几样油还是一箱
Same veggies, same tank of gas

42
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:29,866
因为你本来就只需要那么多
because that's all you ever needed

43
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,733
可有些东西一便宜量就变了
But for some things, cheaper means more

44
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,133
这事我们其实都经历过一回
We've actually all been through this

45
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:36,600
就是手机流量
with mobile data

46
00:01:36,966 --> 00:01:39,300
2014 年 4G 刚出来那会儿
Back in 2014, when 4G just arrived

47
00:01:39,366 --> 00:01:41,666
新华社采访过一位徐先生
Xinhua interviewed a man named Xu

48
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:44,933
为了省流量微博关掉自动加载图片
to save data he turned off photo autoload on Weibo

49
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:47,266
微信关掉视频自动播放
turned off video autoplay on WeChat

50
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,900
到哪儿第一件事都是要 WiFi 密码
and always asked for the WiFi password

51
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:51,600
我估计你也干过
I bet you've done that too

52
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:54,433
后来提速降费到 2019 年
Then came speed-ups and price cuts, and by 2019

53
00:01:54,433 --> 00:01:55,633
手机流量的资费
mobile data rates

54
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:57,900
比 2014 年降了九成多
had dropped over 90% from 2014

55
00:01:58,133 --> 00:01:59,800
那你省下话费了吗
So did you save on your bill

56
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,200
大多数人没有
Most people didn't

57
00:02:01,266 --> 00:02:03,333
因为你开始刷短视频了
because you started scrolling short videos

58
00:02:03,533 --> 00:02:07,466
2014 年每人每月平均用 205 兆流量
In 2014 the average person used 205 MB a month

59
00:02:07,566 --> 00:02:09,733
到 2024 年是 18 个 G
by 2024 it was 18 GB

60
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,333
差不多涨了 90 倍
roughly 90 times as much

61
00:02:11,566 --> 00:02:13,766
中国信通院 2019 年的报告
A 2019 CAICT report

62
00:02:13,766 --> 00:02:14,866
写得很直白
put it bluntly

63
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:18,333
流量用得太猛人均话费没降多少
usage grew so fast your bill barely dropped

64
00:02:18,533 --> 00:02:21,200
所以账单其实是一道乘法
So your bill is really just multiplication

65
00:02:21,366 --> 00:02:22,800
单价乘以用量
unit price times usage

66
00:02:22,933 --> 00:02:24,633
单价是厂商定的
The unit price is set by the company

67
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:26,466
用量是你自己定的
The usage is set by you

68
00:02:26,633 --> 00:02:29,000
降价新闻只告诉了你前一半
A price-cut headline tells half the story

69
00:02:29,233 --> 00:02:31,466
上个月我去听北大的创投课
Last month I took a VC class at Peking University

70
00:02:31,466 --> 00:02:33,100
刘勇老师说得更透
Liu Yong put it more plainly

71
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:35,866
AI 的成本不能只看 token 的单价
you can't judge AI's cost just by the token price

72
00:02:35,966 --> 00:02:38,200
要看做完一件能验收的事
but by what a finished, approved task

73
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:39,500
一共花了多少
costs you in total

74
00:02:39,733 --> 00:02:42,866
AI 做了八成剩下两成要人来补
AI does 80%, a person covers the other 20%

75
00:02:42,866 --> 00:02:44,666
那人工也得算进去
So that labor has to count too

76
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:46,933
AI 现在就是当年的流量
AI right now is just like data back then

77
00:02:46,966 --> 00:02:49,000
说实话我自己就是这样
Honestly, I'm exactly like that

78
00:02:49,033 --> 00:02:50,066
我英语一般
my English is so-so

79
00:02:50,066 --> 00:02:52,500
上个月小米发了一篇英文论文
Last month Xiaomi put out a paper in English

80
00:02:52,566 --> 00:02:53,933
我直接丢给 AI
so I just handed it to AI

81
00:02:53,966 --> 00:02:56,100
让它写了一份精读笔记
and had it write up detailed notes

82
00:02:56,333 --> 00:02:58,533
这种用法放在 AI 贵的时候
This kind of use, back when AI was pricey

83
00:02:58,633 --> 00:02:59,966
没几个人舍得
hardly anyone bothered with it

84
00:03:00,233 --> 00:03:02,000
所以真正要问的是
So the real question is

85
00:03:02,066 --> 00:03:04,733
便宜了以后用量会涨多少
once it's cheaper, how much will usage grow

86
00:03:05,766 --> 00:03:08,200
1865 年英国经济学家杰文斯
In 1865 the British economist Jevons

87
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,366
写了一本书叫煤炭问题
wrote a book called The Coal Question

88
00:03:10,866 --> 00:03:13,600
那会儿英国人担心煤迟早烧光
Back then Britons worried coal would run out

89
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:15,200
很多人觉得不用慌
but many weren't worried

90
00:03:15,566 --> 00:03:18,966
蒸汽机越来越省煤问题自己就解决了
since steam engines would get more efficient and fix it

91
00:03:19,066 --> 00:03:20,500
这话有依据
There was evidence for that

92
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,766
瓦特改良过的蒸汽机干同样的活
Watt's improved engine did the same work

93
00:03:23,966 --> 00:03:26,733
比老式的省下了三分之二以上的煤
and cut coal use by more than two-thirds

94
00:03:26,833 --> 00:03:29,266
可杰文斯说正好相反
But Jevons said it was just the opposite

95
00:03:29,466 --> 00:03:31,766
他的原话翻译过来大意是
Translated, his own words were roughly this

96
00:03:31,866 --> 00:03:34,566
以为节省燃料就等于少烧燃料
to think saving fuel means burning less

97
00:03:34,566 --> 00:03:37,366
是彻底搞混了事实恰恰相反
is a total confusion, and the truth is the opposite

98
00:03:37,533 --> 00:03:39,933
说白了蒸汽机省煤了
Basically, once steam engines saved coal

99
00:03:39,933 --> 00:03:41,500
用它就划算了
they became worth using

100
00:03:41,533 --> 00:03:43,400
以前只有矿井舍得装
At first only mines put them in

101
00:03:43,433 --> 00:03:46,366
后来纺织厂铁厂火车轮船
then textile mills, ironworks, trains, and ships

102
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:47,566
全都装上了
all got one too

103
00:03:47,566 --> 00:03:49,166
英国一年挖的煤
The coal Britain mined each year

104
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:51,533
1750 年大约 500 万吨
was about 5 million tons in 1750

105
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:54,133
到 1850 年是 6000 多万吨
and over 60 million tons by 1850

106
00:03:54,466 --> 00:03:56,066
一百年涨了十多倍
more than tenfold in a century

107
00:03:56,233 --> 00:03:57,766
每一台是省了
Sure, each engine saved coal

108
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,366
可台数涨得更快
but their numbers grew faster

109
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:02,533
后来人们就把这叫作杰文斯悖论
Later, people called this the Jevons paradox

110
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:05,200
效率越高总消耗反而越多
The more efficient, the more use climbs instead

111
00:04:05,566 --> 00:04:08,133
它会不会发生就看一件事
Whether that happens comes down to one thing

112
00:04:08,366 --> 00:04:10,900
便宜了以后用量涨得有多猛
once it's cheaper, how much usage jumps

113
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:12,100
打个比方
Let's say

114
00:04:12,133 --> 00:04:14,266
价格降到原来的四分之一
the price drops to a quarter

115
00:04:14,266 --> 00:04:17,366
用量只翻一倍总花费砍掉一半
If usage only doubles, spending is halved

116
00:04:17,366 --> 00:04:18,966
这才是真省钱
Now that's real savings

117
00:04:19,266 --> 00:04:21,700
用量涨四倍正好打平
If usage quadruples, you break even exactly

118
00:04:21,866 --> 00:04:23,266
用量涨到十倍
If usage goes up tenfold

119
00:04:23,266 --> 00:04:25,533
总花费就变成了原来的两倍半
spending ends up at 2.5 times what it was

120
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:27,366
那 AI 是哪一种
So which one is AI

121
00:04:27,833 --> 00:04:29,600
谷歌每个月处理的 token
Google's monthly token count

122
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,566
两年前是 9点7 万亿
was 9.7 trillion two years ago

123
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:34,566
今年 5 月超过了 3200 万亿
and by this May it topped 3,200 trillion

124
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,466
两年涨了三百多倍
up more than 300 times in two years

125
00:04:36,566 --> 00:04:37,766
钱也跟着涨
The money went up too

126
00:04:37,933 --> 00:04:39,533
光是 Anthropic 一家
Just Anthropic alone

127
00:04:39,533 --> 00:04:41,466
去年的收入就涨了 12 倍
saw its revenue jump 12 times last year

128
00:04:41,633 --> 00:04:43,666
而且不光是事情变多了
And it's not just more things happening

129
00:04:43,666 --> 00:04:45,933
一件事本身也越用越多
each task itself is using more too

130
00:04:46,166 --> 00:04:47,933
DeepSeek 的一个便宜模型
DeepSeek has a cheap model

131
00:04:47,933 --> 00:04:49,766
新版本答题更准了
the new version got more accurate

132
00:04:49,933 --> 00:04:52,466
可每道题的成本反而涨了两倍半
but the cost per question actually rose 2.5 times

133
00:04:52,633 --> 00:04:55,300
因为现在的 AI 会多想一会儿
Because today's AI thinks a little longer

134
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,800
想得越久用掉的 token 就越多
the longer it thinks, the more tokens it burns

135
00:04:58,066 --> 00:04:59,066
去年 1 月
Last January

136
00:04:59,066 --> 00:05:01,066
DeepSeek 的便宜模型一出来
when DeepSeek's cheap model came out

137
00:05:01,066 --> 00:05:03,966
大家担心以后用不了那么多算力
people worried we'd need way less computing power

138
00:05:04,166 --> 00:05:05,600
微软的 CEO 纳德拉
Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella

139
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:07,533
那天凌晨发了一条推文
posted a tweet in the wee hours that day

140
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,600
杰文斯悖论又来了
Jevons paradox strikes again

141
00:05:09,666 --> 00:05:12,566
他说AI 越高效越容易用
He said as AI gets more efficient and accessible

142
00:05:12,633 --> 00:05:14,066
用量就会暴涨
we'll see its use skyrocket

143
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,800
变成一样我们怎么都用不够的东西
turning it into a commodity we just can't get enough of

144
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,933
他是卖算力的当然希望这样
He sells compute, so of course he'd want that

145
00:05:20,066 --> 00:05:22,700
但这两年的数确实站在他那边
But the numbers these past two years back him up

146
00:05:22,866 --> 00:05:24,033
Anthropic 有个
Anthropic has a

147
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:25,666
200 美元的包月套餐
$200 monthly plan

148
00:05:25,833 --> 00:05:27,166
去年有个用户
Last year one user

149
00:05:27,166 --> 00:05:30,166
在这个套餐上跑掉了几万美元的用量
burned through tens of thousands of dollars in usage

150
00:05:30,333 --> 00:05:32,466
逼得他们加了每周限额
forcing them to add weekly limits

151
00:05:32,866 --> 00:05:34,100
司马光说过
Sima Guang once said

152
00:05:34,133 --> 00:05:36,800
由俭入奢易由奢入俭难
thrift to luxury is easy, luxury to thrift is hard

153
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,566
用法一旦被撑大
Once your usage stretches wider

154
00:05:38,566 --> 00:05:40,400
就很难再缩回去了
it's hard to shrink it back down

155
00:05:41,466 --> 00:05:43,366
那是不是所有东西降价
So does that mean every price cut

156
00:05:43,366 --> 00:05:44,966
最后都会越花越多
always ends up costing you more

157
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,000
也不是
Not always

158
00:05:46,266 --> 00:05:48,700
盐降价一半你不会多吃一倍
Salt at half price, you won't eat twice as much

159
00:05:48,866 --> 00:05:51,400
杰文斯悖论只发生在一种东西上
The Jevons paradox only hits one kind of thing

160
00:05:51,566 --> 00:05:54,100
便宜一点就能冒出新用法
where a little cheaper sparks new uses

161
00:05:54,433 --> 00:05:56,666
煤是这样流量是这样
Coal was like that, so was data

162
00:05:56,666 --> 00:05:58,366
现在的 AI 也是这样
and now AI is too

163
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:00,433
所以下次再看到降价
So next time you see a price cut

164
00:06:00,433 --> 00:06:02,166
先别急着算能省多少
don't rush to count the savings

165
00:06:02,266 --> 00:06:03,300
多问一句
ask one more thing

166
00:06:03,466 --> 00:06:05,866
便宜了以后我会不会用得更多
once it's cheaper, will I use more

167
00:06:06,166 --> 00:06:07,266
如果答案是会
If the answer is yes

168
00:06:07,266 --> 00:06:09,600
那就别盯着单价算总账
then skip the unit price, add up the total

169
00:06:09,733 --> 00:06:12,366
一个月最多花多少到了就停
Set a monthly cap, stop once you hit it

170
00:06:12,566 --> 00:06:15,600
一件事做完一共花了多少值不值
For each task, add up the cost, worth it or not

171
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,766
当然多花的钱也不一定是坏事
Of course, spending more isn't always a bad thing

172
00:06:18,866 --> 00:06:21,333
当年英国人买煤越买越多
Back then, the British bought more and more coal

173
00:06:21,333 --> 00:06:23,766
换回来的是一整场工业革命
and got back a whole Industrial Revolution

174
00:06:23,833 --> 00:06:26,433
真正要看的是多花的这部分
What really matters is whether that extra spending

175
00:06:26,433 --> 00:06:28,200
有没有换回更多的东西
bought you something more

176
00:06:28,633 --> 00:06:29,966
我自己打算这周
I'm planning this week

177
00:06:29,966 --> 00:06:31,766
就把 AI 的账单拉出来
to pull up my AI bill

178
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:32,733
不看单价
skip the unit price

179
00:06:32,833 --> 00:06:35,500
按一件事一件事重新算一遍
and redo the math task by task

180
00:06:35,766 --> 00:06:38,100
回到 10 月 8 号早上那条新闻
Back to that news from the morning of October 8

181
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:39,300
那 百分之75
That 75%

182
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:41,466
没有让谁的账单变薄
didn't make anyone's bill thinner

183
00:06:41,666 --> 00:06:43,700
